  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is fast (24 h regulator, 48 h customer) but its scope is limited to serious events (thermal runaway, fire, explosion, venting), leaving smoke/minor overheating and pre-investigation reporting out. S2 keeps the 55 °C test and a 5% limit but never stops sales above it (corrective action plus annual retesting and regulator discretion), which saves Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2% while still giving buyers the numeric failure rate and keeping it out of general publication (both NW-1 and HC-1 respected). S3 (6-year retrofit with required alternatives) and S4 (built-in suppression at 36 months) sit inside the acceptable ranges and honour NW-2/HC-2, while S5's mandatory 8/100k recall with immediate customer notice squarely hits Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9/100k."
 },
